{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-finite-type}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:56fd110cd45715427466228dd1acdfe0f0572106daa876b92e49418498a9684c", "source_text": "Morphisms of finite type", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8fb076b25260871f74d9b2117fe37d1f13296fcb62c9a699f93560ab8dd376b1", "unit_id": "tag:01T0:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$R[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]$", "MATH_0004": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-finite-type}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae718a5b4636ab133785dcf61bf55aaee128d4165cd4a424d688765b81799f69", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd52bbd06fb85709ed97464d07a87adea2662790defdb01f07aade4b3b032596", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring map <MATH_0001> is said to be of finite type if\n<MATH_0002> is isomorphic to a quotient of <MATH_0003> as an <MATH_0004>-algebra, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dba0e8c6cbd2125b4d09d97a861f78455bdc35f259e4ca3243dd0b3cf42d5b68", "unit_id": "tag:01T0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(A) = U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(R) = V \\subset S$", "MATH_0007": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0008": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:68dd16c2cbe8006bf68f241c73cccf0a9fe9704b4f68a41eeb6d1d1ceda277c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cbc7fc714579e39fb5e0104d7188ed9ba0b076bfa13ceffaaecac0c35ed29b31", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say that <MATH_0002> is of <TEXTITOPEN_0001>finite type at <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nthere exists an affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0004>\nof <MATH_0005> and an affine open <MATH_0006>\nwith <MATH_0007> such that the induced ring map\n<MATH_0008> is of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say that <MATH_0009> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>locally of finite type<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if it is\nof finite type at every point of <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say that <MATH_0011> is of <TEXTITOPEN_0003>finite type<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if it is locally of\nfinite type and quasi-compact.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4867044a2270dce232a6b4a7f478a7a1a831aa20fbabcf54be700ca593cbbb28", "unit_id": "tag:01T1:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0007": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0008": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0009": "$U_i \\to V_j$", "MATH_0010": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0011": "$S = \\bigcup_{j \\in J} V_j$", "MATH_0012": "$f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup_{i \\in I_j} U_i$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(V_j) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0014": "$j\\in J, i\\in I_j$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0017": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0018": "$f(U) \\subset V$", "MATH_0019": "$f|_U : U \\to V$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-finite-type-characterize}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:831157cffc4f322e7a359b1d2895997bfe94b41d1a431cf27d30599a8144b2c2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6eba48009b161ea90f1804c738f45caa44fee07d02368048b51deb52e632ebd9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is locally of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0003> For all affine opens <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004>\nwith <MATH_0005> the ring map\n<MATH_0006> is of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exist an open covering <MATH_0007>\nand open coverings <MATH_0008> such\nthat each of the morphisms <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>\nis locally of finite type.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exist an affine open covering <MATH_0011>\nand affine open coverings <MATH_0012> such\nthat the ring map <MATH_0013> is\nof finite type, for all <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0015> is locally of finite type then for\nany open subschemes <MATH_0016>, <MATH_0017> with <MATH_0018>\nthe restriction <MATH_0019> is locally of finite type.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:881df813cdfbfe9b1cda91099885288344b6756b23e69fcdca7f7f5ef11338e9", "unit_id": "tag:01T2:statement"}
